@* A showroom business's demo (F128.2, in the showroom since F127.1): its stage in its colour, and its conversation
   played on a mock of its own website with its sample brand, nothing else beside it, so the agent is what the visitor
   watches (FX194). The business is made up and says so; the conversation is real, recorded once, and once it has
   played the visitor can try the agent live (F127.2). *@
<DemoStage Accent="Accent" Topic="@KickerLine" Fills="true">
    <Title>@Heading</Title>
    <Summary>
        @Summary <span class="stage-made-up">@Business is a made-up business. The conversation is real, recorded once
            and played back. Nothing runs while you watch.</span>
    </Summary>
    <Player>
        <SiteMock @ref="_mock" Address="@Address" Business="@Business" Colours="Colours" Font="Font" Mark="Mark"
                  Tagline="@Tagline"
                  HeroLine="@HeroLine" HeroNote="@HeroNote" AgentLabel="@AgentLabel" Look="Look"
                  HeroPhoto="@HeroPhoto" HeroPhotoAlt="@HeroPhotoAlt" HeroAction="@HeroAction" Facts="Facts"
                  Pages="Pages" Shown="@_shown" Went="Go" Live="_trying" Header="Header">
            <Agent>
                @* Trying it (F127.2): the business's agent live in the same corner, until the visitor goes back. *@
                @if (_trying)
                {
                    <MockLiveChat Identity="@Identity" Hint="@Hint" Placeholder="@($"Ask {Business}…")"
                                  ToolCalled="Show" Left="Watch" Asked="_asked" />
                }
                else
                {
                    @* At a person's pace (Louis: "slow it down like realtime"): the agent writes at an easy reading
                       speed, and the visitor's next question comes after a breath, as they read and type. It waits
                       while the site's guide talks (F134.4), and it starts only when asked (F160, Louis: "do not
                       make it autoplay"), by the visitor's Play or by the guide showing one of its turns. Once it has played,
                       the visitor can try it themselves. *@
                    <RecordedChat @ref="_recorded" Turns="Turns" Title="@Address" PlayAgain="Play it again"
                                  Place="@ConversationPlace"
                                  Start="RecordedStart.WhenAsked" Play="Play the conversation" PlayOn="Play on"
                                  ShowWork="false" Pace="2.5" TurnGap="2200" TurnStarted="Reach" ToolCalled="Show"
                                  Hold="GuideTalking" TryIt="@Words.TryItYourself" Tried="Try" />
                }
            </Agent>
        </SiteMock>
    </Player>
</DemoStage>
